WEBVTT

00:00.340 --> 00:03.887
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.888 --> 00:07.171
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.172 --> 00:10.740
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.741 --> 00:13.741
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.742 --> 00:17.242
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.243 --> 00:20.643
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.644 --> 00:22.210
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.211 --> 00:23.611
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.612 --> 00:29.252
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.982 --> 00:35.616
Hi. It's me, Peter.

00:35.617 --> 00:38.113
You may be wondering
what I'm doing in a library.

00:38.114 --> 00:40.517
Well, I actually drove my car
into this rich guy's house,

00:40.518 --> 00:42.952
and he locked me in here
until the police come.

00:42.953 --> 00:44.284
Don't believe me?

00:44.285 --> 00:46.600
I don't know. I just
locked him in the library.

00:46.601 --> 00:48.920
Seems like he's on something.
He's got crazy eyes

00:48.921 --> 00:50.754
and keeps screaming,
"I don't care."

00:50.755 --> 00:52.021
I don't care!

00:52.022 --> 00:53.588
Anyway, I've got
some time to kill

00:53.589 --> 00:55.423
before this room
is filled with tear gas,

00:55.424 --> 00:57.189
so I thought,
"Why not finally read

00:57.190 --> 00:59.724
some of the classics
I never read in high school."

00:59.725 --> 01:02.158
<i>Here's one right here,
The Great Gatsby.</i>

01:02.159 --> 01:06.193
A book by the only respected guy
in the world named Scott.

01:18.983 --> 01:21.831
<i>It was my first
summer staying at the shore,</i>

01:21.832 --> 01:25.167
<i>but I had a feeling that I,
Nick "The Situation" Carraway,</i>

01:25.168 --> 01:26.833
<i>would fit right in.</i>

01:29.369 --> 01:31.402
<i>Hey, it's Nick
from The Great Gatsby.</i>

01:31.403 --> 01:34.769
I just checked in, and somebody
left their teeth here.

01:34.770 --> 01:37.571
I-I don't know,
it's just a set of teeth.

01:37.572 --> 01:39.404
I-I guess men's?

01:39.405 --> 01:41.173
No, I'm not putting them
anywhere.

01:41.174 --> 01:42.872
You come and get them.

01:42.873 --> 01:45.941
Yecch. The neighbors are having a party

01:45.942 --> 01:47.641
with loud jazz music.

01:47.642 --> 01:49.875
Well, at least
annoyingly scatting over jazz

01:49.876 --> 01:51.443
hasn't been invented yet.

01:55.778 --> 01:58.128
Oh, that must have
been invented today!

02:11.302 --> 02:12.817
Hey, whose party is this?

02:12.818 --> 02:15.618
I'm not sure. Women aren't
allowed to ask questions yet.

02:15.619 --> 02:17.018
So, what's your name?

02:17.019 --> 02:18.786
Madam, you forget yourself.

02:23.173 --> 02:25.355
<i>That's when I first
laid eyes on him.</i>

02:25.356 --> 02:26.889
<i>Jay Gatsby.</i>

02:26.890 --> 02:29.056
<i>He was clearly playing with
himself through his pocket,</i>

02:29.057 --> 02:30.590
<i>but I pretended not to see.</i>

02:30.591 --> 02:31.891
Hello. Welcome
to my party.

02:31.892 --> 02:33.891
Name's Gatsby. Good to
meet you, old sport.

02:33.892 --> 02:35.325
Yeah, just a wave is fine.

02:35.326 --> 02:37.225
I-I'm your new neighbor,
Nick Carraway.

02:37.226 --> 02:39.227
Oh, I hope we weren't
too loud, old sport.

02:39.228 --> 02:40.861
Yeah, this
"old sport" thing,

02:40.862 --> 02:42.728
is this... is this something
you're trying out,

02:42.729 --> 02:44.762
- or is this a keeper?
- I just met you,

02:44.763 --> 02:46.730
so I want to tell you
something very private.

02:46.731 --> 02:48.130
Let's go out to the dock.

02:51.917 --> 02:53.832
I come down here
to think every night

02:53.833 --> 02:55.499
and gaze at that green light.

02:55.500 --> 02:57.633
It's where the love
of my life lives,

02:57.634 --> 02:59.017
Daisy Buchanan.

03:01.253 --> 03:02.868
Um, I hate to
break it to you,

03:02.869 --> 03:04.370
but that light you've
been looking at

03:04.371 --> 03:06.336
is a gay gym called
The Pump House.

03:06.337 --> 03:09.804
I-I only know that because I saw a
coupon that came with my rental.

03:09.805 --> 03:12.372
Um... anyway, Daisy's
house is over there.

03:12.373 --> 03:14.739
- She's my cousin.
- Daisy's your cousin?!

03:14.740 --> 03:18.174
Yeah. Lot of weird coincidences
for an American classic, huh?

03:18.175 --> 03:19.707
Wha... I have to see her!

03:19.708 --> 03:21.008
Well, I can set that up.

03:21.009 --> 03:22.609
Um, only thing is she's married.

03:22.610 --> 03:25.076
Yeah, and I hear
her husband's a real heel.

03:25.077 --> 03:26.811
Whoa-hoa! Language!

03:26.812 --> 03:28.277
But yeah, I'll set it up.

03:28.278 --> 03:30.679
Um, tea tomorrow at
my house, 2:00 p.m.

03:30.680 --> 03:33.480
Great. She's...
she's gonna be there, right?

03:33.481 --> 03:34.847
Yeah. Why wouldn't
she be there?

03:34.848 --> 03:37.547
I don't know, I'm just getting
a funny vibe from you.

03:37.548 --> 03:39.549
You asked me down
to the docks alone,

03:39.550 --> 03:42.549
<i>and you're getting
a funny vibe from me?</i>

03:46.903 --> 03:49.185
Wow. What an ugly
little house.

03:49.186 --> 03:52.552
<i>Oh, yeah, it's not that palace
of domestic abuse you live in.</i>

03:52.553 --> 03:54.820
Whassup...?

03:54.821 --> 03:57.287
Oh, my God! Is it really you?

03:57.288 --> 04:00.804
Oh, I've missed you, Daisy.
You're as beautiful as ever.

04:00.806 --> 04:01.957
You know what else
is beautiful?

04:01.958 --> 04:03.758
My bank account. Boom!

04:03.759 --> 04:05.824
- Rich guy.
- You're rich now?

04:05.825 --> 04:07.992
- Oh, my God, I love that!
- I know, right?

04:07.993 --> 04:09.925
Come on, I'll show
you my place.

04:09.926 --> 04:11.026
Oh, you're leaving?

04:11.027 --> 04:13.027
But I made
all these deviled eggs.

04:13.028 --> 04:15.194
<i>- You made?
- You know what I meant.</i>

04:15.195 --> 04:17.495
Yeah, you made them.
Great job.

04:28.318 --> 04:30.833
You know, one of the best parts
of having an enormous mansion

04:30.834 --> 04:33.402
is being able to come out here
and get some fresh air.

04:33.403 --> 04:35.735
You know, sometimes I just want
to jump off this balcony

04:35.736 --> 04:37.619
and into that pool down there.

04:39.155 --> 04:40.270
So do it.

04:40.271 --> 04:41.938
Yeah, I know, right?
Do it!

04:41.939 --> 04:43.171
Yeah. Do it.

04:43.172 --> 04:45.038
I know. I totally should,
right? Here I go.

04:45.039 --> 04:46.572
One, two, three...

04:46.573 --> 04:48.473
Whoa!
Can you imagine?

04:48.474 --> 04:50.408
Yeah, I-I can imagine.
It would be fun.

04:50.409 --> 04:52.975
- You should do it.
- If only it were that easy, right?

04:52.976 --> 04:54.643
It is. It looks
deep enough.

04:54.644 --> 04:56.309
It's your pool.
It's your house.

04:56.310 --> 04:58.310
- You can do whatever you want.
- I know, right?

04:58.311 --> 05:00.010
Ah, you know what?
I can't right now.

05:00.011 --> 05:01.278
My pool guy's cleaning it.

05:01.279 --> 05:04.379
Are you going to bone her?

05:09.633 --> 05:11.015
This is amazing!

05:11.016 --> 05:13.282
I've never seen
so many shirts.

05:13.283 --> 05:15.383
D-Do you have enough to,
you know, throw?

05:15.384 --> 05:17.517
Yeah, you know, they're
actually kind of expensive...

05:17.518 --> 05:18.785
Ah, there she goes.

05:18.786 --> 05:22.219
Shirt! Shirt! Shirt!

05:22.220 --> 05:24.119
Shirt! Shirt!

05:24.120 --> 05:25.353
Okay, five is good.

05:25.354 --> 05:26.788
Five is-is probably good.

05:26.789 --> 05:28.287
Shirt! Shirt!

05:28.288 --> 05:29.655
Were you, uh...

05:29.656 --> 05:32.538
were-were you this crazy
when we dated before?

05:37.509 --> 05:39.159
Mm, Gatsby, is it?

05:39.160 --> 05:41.726
I've been hearing about your
vast newly acquired wealth

05:41.727 --> 05:43.727
and your attentions
to my wife.

05:43.728 --> 05:45.660
So I thought I would
have you over

05:45.661 --> 05:47.328
to my equally
large and fancy

05:47.329 --> 05:49.328
but imperceptibly
more classy mansion

05:49.329 --> 05:50.629
for an awkward dinner.

05:50.630 --> 05:52.763
And, Nick, have
you met Jordan?

05:52.764 --> 05:56.698
She plays golf, and is what kids
will someday call a "DUFF."

05:56.699 --> 05:58.799
Hey, yeah.
Nice tam-o'-shanter.

05:58.800 --> 06:01.100
I'll drink your finger bowl
if you don't want it.

06:01.101 --> 06:04.101
<i>In the book, I actually
go on a few dates with Jordan.</i>

06:04.102 --> 06:05.701
<i>We're gonna skip all that.</i>

06:05.702 --> 06:07.835
Anyway, like I was saying,
you're a trash,

06:07.836 --> 06:10.769
'cause you earned your money a
little bit more recently than me.

06:10.770 --> 06:13.504
- What are you getting at?
- I'm saying I invited you over

06:13.505 --> 06:15.371
and sat you next
to my wife to say,

06:15.372 --> 06:17.072
"Stay away from my wife!"

06:17.073 --> 06:18.206
You know what we should do?

06:18.207 --> 06:19.706
Let's all drunk-drive
into Manhattan

06:19.707 --> 06:21.107
and get a hotel room

06:21.108 --> 06:22.673
and have the same conversation
we're having here.

06:22.674 --> 06:25.258
I'm starting to think this
isn't a very good book.

06:27.827 --> 06:29.811
I'd like to add another bit
of pointless confusion

06:29.812 --> 06:31.110
that will make sense later.

06:31.111 --> 06:33.077
Let's everyone drive
somebody else's car.

06:33.078 --> 06:34.560
Someone can take my coupe.

06:34.561 --> 06:35.979
I'm riding with Gatsby,
I don't care which car.

06:35.980 --> 06:37.313
I'll take someone
in Daisy's car.

06:37.314 --> 06:39.147
I don't think Daisy said
you could drive her car.

06:39.148 --> 06:40.613
Tom, why don't you take
Jay's car?

06:40.614 --> 06:42.115
- Who's Jay?
- Gatsby.

06:42.116 --> 06:44.482
Okay, I have never heard
anyone call him that.

06:44.483 --> 06:47.300
Look, if you're in your own car
you're in the wrong car.

06:55.237 --> 06:56.853
All right,
you guys get gas.

06:56.854 --> 06:58.720
I got to talk to this
random mechanic's horny wife

06:58.721 --> 06:59.888
about some business.

06:59.889 --> 07:01.888
Wilson? Gonna need
to fill 'er up!

07:01.889 --> 07:04.839
Wilson's wife? Fill 'er up?
Get it?

07:10.559 --> 07:12.758
I don't know what
they do up there,

07:12.759 --> 07:15.593
but they sure do listen
to Def Leppard pretty loud.

07:18.428 --> 07:21.662
So, seen any good movies lately?

07:21.663 --> 07:24.330
<i>We just saw Woman Tied
to Railroad Tracks 5.</i>

07:24.331 --> 07:25.896
Pretty similar to 4.

07:25.897 --> 07:28.031
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

07:28.032 --> 07:30.431
Wow, looks like you guys
are getting a head start

07:30.432 --> 07:31.866
on the Depression here.

07:33.733 --> 07:36.167
Thanks for stopping
by, Mr. Buchanan.

07:36.168 --> 07:38.835
Yeah, sure. Don't tell anyone
how bad I look naked.

07:38.836 --> 07:41.937
Have fun raising my bastard.

07:41.938 --> 07:43.169
All right,
let's head out.

07:43.170 --> 07:44.671
Wait, but first
I want to see

07:44.672 --> 07:46.270
if we're in the
funny horn era.

07:46.271 --> 07:48.788
Ah-ooga! Ah-ha! We are!

07:52.825 --> 07:55.274
All right, Gatsby,
you think you're so hot?

07:55.275 --> 07:58.609
Let me show you how a classy guy
does classy stuff.

07:58.610 --> 08:00.409
Hello, room service?
I'd like a bottle

08:00.410 --> 08:02.909
of your
second most expensive champagne.

08:02.910 --> 08:06.145
<i>And I'd like your
most expensive bottle.</i>

08:06.146 --> 08:08.212
Wow. Walked right
into that one.

08:08.213 --> 08:10.847
Okay, fine. Well, then let's
see who has higher socks.

08:10.848 --> 08:12.180
Nya-ha!

08:12.181 --> 08:14.181
Whatever, Tom.
None of that matters.

08:14.182 --> 08:15.681
<i>Daisy's in love with me.</i>

08:15.682 --> 08:17.850
<i>In fact, she's never loved you.</i>

08:17.851 --> 08:19.283
Oh, is that so?

08:19.284 --> 08:22.785
Well, I hear Gatsby didn't
even fight in World War I.

08:22.786 --> 08:24.318
Wait, why is he calling it that?

08:24.319 --> 08:26.035
<i>Is there gonna be
another big war?</i>

08:27.472 --> 08:29.019
I'm sorry, Tom.

08:29.020 --> 08:31.020
That's right.
I'm in love with Daisy,

08:31.021 --> 08:33.204
and she loves me, old sport.

08:34.240 --> 08:36.522
Would anyone like
a deviled egg

08:36.523 --> 08:39.307
from a tea I had
several days ago?

08:42.643 --> 08:44.226
Well, that was awful.

08:44.227 --> 08:46.426
But I sure do enjoy
driving your car

08:46.427 --> 08:48.160
instead of you driving it,

08:48.161 --> 08:50.161
even though we came
in a different car.

08:50.162 --> 08:52.095
Drunk. Don't forget drunk.

08:52.096 --> 08:54.178
You're drunk-driving my car.

08:56.114 --> 08:57.363
Gas and sandwiches!

08:57.364 --> 08:59.831
Get your gas and sandwiches!

09:02.617 --> 09:06.783
Oh, that must be Tom, since
I saw him in that car earlier!

09:08.018 --> 09:10.435
Tom! Tom! It's me!

09:13.437 --> 09:14.836
Oh-ho, no!

09:14.837 --> 09:16.203
Myrtle!

09:16.204 --> 09:18.337
Where will I ever
find another woman

09:18.338 --> 09:21.355
with a hotter name
than Myrtle?

09:25.493 --> 09:27.875
All right, pool,
do your thing.

09:27.876 --> 09:30.641
<i>You hungover?
Uh, a little bit, yeah.</i>

09:30.642 --> 09:33.543
Okay, we're sort of racing
to the end here.

09:33.544 --> 09:35.810
And with that,
I shall step

09:35.811 --> 09:37.879
slightly out of range.

09:37.880 --> 09:40.496
All right, I'm just
gonna take a quick swim.

09:41.531 --> 09:43.312
Oh, my God!
Where are the stairs?

09:43.313 --> 09:45.630
There's no stairs!
I'm never gonna make it!

09:47.533 --> 09:49.682
You were standing
earlier in the day

09:49.683 --> 09:51.932
next to the car
that hit my wife.

09:58.786 --> 10:01.686
<i>I would soon return
to New York a changed man,</i>

10:01.687 --> 10:04.387
<i>because, for me,
that will always be the summer</i>

10:04.388 --> 10:06.989
<i>that I finally put my head
underwater.</i>

10:06.990 --> 10:09.322
I did it! I did it!

10:09.323 --> 10:11.206
Aw, I wish somebody
had seen that.

10:16.916 --> 10:18.231
Hi. Me again.

10:18.232 --> 10:20.033
I'm not
in that guy's library anymore.

10:20.034 --> 10:22.534
I snuck up to the attic
just before the cops busted in.

10:22.535 --> 10:24.484
They're down there now. Look.

10:27.020 --> 10:29.003
Only problem is,
I really want to get

10:29.004 --> 10:31.270
to that trunk of costumes
in the corner.

10:31.271 --> 10:34.204
On the one hand, I don't want
to give away my location.

10:34.205 --> 10:37.039
On the other hand,
there might be a pirate hat.

10:40.192 --> 10:42.307
Hmm, no pirate hat,
but I'll make it work.

10:42.308 --> 10:45.042
Argh! I'm a chef
aboard a pirate ship!

10:45.043 --> 10:47.176
Now, who be wantin' pancakes?

10:47.177 --> 10:48.910
I think I hear
something in the attic.

10:48.911 --> 10:50.910
Oh, crap.
While I figure out my options,

10:50.911 --> 10:52.578
<i>here's Huckleberry Finn.</i>

11:01.466 --> 11:03.448
Hi, Huckleberry Finn!

11:03.449 --> 11:05.049
Hi, Tom Sawyer.

11:05.050 --> 11:06.983
You're Tom, I'm Huck.

11:06.984 --> 11:08.316
Everybody good? Yup?

11:08.317 --> 11:09.651
All right, let's do this.

11:09.652 --> 11:12.251
Huckleberry Finn, you get inside
this house this minute.

11:12.252 --> 11:14.720
It's Tuesday morning.
It's time for church.

11:14.721 --> 11:15.919
Aw, Widow Douglas,

11:15.920 --> 11:18.121
I already been to church
three times today.

11:18.122 --> 11:20.605
I want to stay home
and play Angry Birds.

11:25.558 --> 11:27.557
This is addictive.

11:27.558 --> 11:29.358
Hey, I'm your abusive dad,

11:29.359 --> 11:32.025
and I've been drinkin' all
day from this here jug.

11:32.026 --> 11:34.526
Oh, my God, is that
a jug full of porn?

11:34.527 --> 11:36.460
Hey, Widow Douglas,
I want to live with my dad!

11:36.461 --> 11:37.461
Shut your hole!

11:37.462 --> 11:39.061
Now come on,
I need to use your pee.

11:39.062 --> 11:41.678
I'm taking a wagon test
in the morning.

11:43.815 --> 11:46.464
I wish you wouldn't
drink so much.

11:46.465 --> 11:47.932
Stop countin' my drinks!

11:47.933 --> 11:50.082
Now get over here
so I can whip you!

11:51.117 --> 11:53.633
Ow! Pap! No!

11:53.634 --> 11:55.234
Yeah, that's
right, bitch.

11:55.235 --> 11:56.701
Now it's your turn...

11:58.036 --> 12:00.370
Geez, this is worse
than the Widow Douglas' house.

12:00.371 --> 12:01.652
I got to get out of here.

12:04.089 --> 12:06.270
I know. I'll fake my own death.

12:06.271 --> 12:08.739
I just need enough blood
to make it look real.

12:08.740 --> 12:10.272
Hey there!
You must be Huck.

12:10.273 --> 12:11.473
Great to finally
meet you.

12:11.474 --> 12:12.674
I hope you
like it here.

12:12.675 --> 12:14.207
I'm gonna stab you
for your blood.

12:14.208 --> 12:17.009
Oh, come on! I just got shot
in the pool in the last one.

12:22.462 --> 12:25.679
I can't remember
why I needed the blood.

12:32.633 --> 12:34.348
Lord, I'm-a tell ya,

12:34.349 --> 12:36.482
being a slave is
a much worse job

12:36.483 --> 12:38.484
than the temp agency
made it sound.

12:38.485 --> 12:40.017
You gonna eat
all that possum?

12:40.018 --> 12:41.817
I am. My name's Huck Finn.

12:41.818 --> 12:43.218
What's half of your name?

12:43.219 --> 12:44.885
Jim. Nice to meet you.

12:44.886 --> 12:46.486
I'm a runaway slave.

12:46.487 --> 12:48.086
I'm runnin' away
'cause people want me

12:48.087 --> 12:49.820
to wear shoes
and comb my hair.

12:49.821 --> 12:52.504
So I guess we got
the exact same problem.

12:55.540 --> 12:57.657
Hey, what's that sound?

12:57.658 --> 13:00.324
Oh, no!
It sounds like...

13:00.325 --> 13:03.393
a waterfall!

13:03.394 --> 13:05.359
Hold on!

13:13.747 --> 13:16.014
<i>We died.</i>

13:17.715 --> 13:19.197
<i>So wait.
We didn't die?</i>

13:19.198 --> 13:21.247
I don't know.
It's all just jokes.

13:28.220 --> 13:29.768
- Ah! Did you see that?
- What?

13:29.769 --> 13:31.869
I just skipped that
rock six times!

13:31.870 --> 13:33.536
That's a once-in-
a-lifetime skip!

13:33.537 --> 13:35.737
- That's nice.
- You don't believe me, do ya?

13:35.738 --> 13:38.071
I believe we've been
out here a long time,

13:38.072 --> 13:40.873
and a man's mind begins
to play tricks on him.

13:40.874 --> 13:42.105
It happened for real!

13:42.106 --> 13:44.240
I can't believe
you didn't see it!

13:44.241 --> 13:45.840
<i>Of course I saw it.</i>

13:45.841 --> 13:48.709
<i>Most amazing damn thing
I ever did witness.</i>

13:48.710 --> 13:51.043
<i>But I wasn't gonna tell Huck,
'cause he claimed</i>

13:51.044 --> 13:53.577
<i>he didn't see me hook-shot
that apple core</i>

13:53.578 --> 13:56.245
<i>into the garbage
from way far away.</i>

13:56.246 --> 13:58.011
Hello, friends.

13:58.012 --> 14:00.079
Why are you so friendly?
You con men?

14:00.080 --> 14:01.613
No, we're businessmen.

14:01.614 --> 14:03.614
We're fake-selling
the Brooklyn Bridge.

14:03.615 --> 14:05.014
Don't say
"fake-selling."

14:05.015 --> 14:07.114
We're real-selling
the Brooklyn Bridge.

14:07.115 --> 14:08.416
Stop qualifying
the selling.

14:08.417 --> 14:10.083
We're just selling
the Brooklyn Bridge.

14:10.084 --> 14:11.916
- I'll buy it.
- Hold on, now, Huck.

14:11.917 --> 14:13.850
<i>These fellas
are con men.</i>

14:13.851 --> 14:15.418
Push off,
you grifters.

14:15.419 --> 14:17.485
We don't want
to ever see you again.

14:17.486 --> 14:19.035
Fine, we're going!

14:22.272 --> 14:25.088
It's a river... we can't
control how fast it goes.

14:25.089 --> 14:27.105
We can barely steer!

14:31.043 --> 14:32.524
Sorry.

14:36.376 --> 14:38.926
Hey, what if it's spelled
with an A at the end of it?

14:38.927 --> 14:40.160
Is that okay?

14:40.161 --> 14:42.611
Jim? Jim?

14:45.113 --> 14:46.996
Jim? Jim?

14:46.997 --> 14:50.397
If you're looking for a gym,
Ye Olde Pump House is that way.

14:50.398 --> 14:53.365
Can't miss it.
Green light on a dock.

14:53.366 --> 14:56.732
Tom Sawyer? What are you
doing so far from home?

14:56.733 --> 14:58.734
Rush is playing
here tonight.

14:58.735 --> 15:00.734
They wrote a
song about me.

15:00.735 --> 15:03.069
Oh. Well, I'm looking
for my friend, Jim.

15:03.070 --> 15:05.269
Huck! Great news!
I'm free!

15:05.270 --> 15:07.537
You are? That's awesome!
When did that happen?

15:07.538 --> 15:09.203
It's just being
revealed now,

15:09.204 --> 15:11.471
but it happened
hundreds of pages ago.

15:11.472 --> 15:13.138
Oh. Huh. Weird.

15:13.139 --> 15:15.306
So, uh, what's left to do?

15:15.307 --> 15:16.807
I'll tell you what:

15:16.808 --> 15:18.374
Rush concert!

15:29.446 --> 15:31.778
Hey. I'm Mark Twain.

15:31.779 --> 15:33.447
Pretty cool book, huh?

15:36.382 --> 15:38.759
Well, while I'm being
booked and processed downtown,

15:38.760 --> 15:42.032
we have time for one more
classic of American literature.

15:42.033 --> 15:44.282
This one's about
idiots choking rodents.

15:44.283 --> 15:46.384
<i>I give you Of Mice and Men.</i>

15:46.385 --> 15:48.418
- Read him his rights.
- You know what?

15:48.419 --> 15:50.419
I'm like to read 'em myself.

15:50.420 --> 15:53.520
"Chapter one:
eat my ass, pigs."

15:53.521 --> 15:55.770
Aah! The bones in my nose!

16:03.708 --> 16:08.491
Wow. I remember when this used
to be all orange groves.

16:08.492 --> 16:11.775
It's... it's currently
all orange groves.

16:15.012 --> 16:17.294
Tell me again about
our dream, George.

16:17.295 --> 16:18.696
All right, all right.

16:18.697 --> 16:21.096
We're going to open a
bed-and-breakfast in the country,

16:21.097 --> 16:23.698
and we won't be afraid
to let our guests know

16:23.699 --> 16:25.898
<i>that we are Steelers fans
in this house.</i>

16:25.899 --> 16:28.799
- What about the rabbits?
- Yeah, we'll have rabbits, too.

16:28.800 --> 16:31.133
But we'll also have a sign
in the front that says,

16:31.134 --> 16:33.233
"Steelers fan parking only."

16:33.234 --> 16:35.902
And sometimes we'll give
our guests a fake hard time.

16:35.903 --> 16:38.169
Like if they're Jets fans,
we'll be all like,

16:38.170 --> 16:40.303
"Okay,
I hope you don't get towed."

16:40.304 --> 16:41.470
But obviously, you know,

16:41.471 --> 16:43.187
of course, we're
not gonna tow 'em.

16:53.060 --> 16:54.240
Hey there, strangers.

16:54.241 --> 16:55.909
Welcome to Phelps Ranch.

16:55.910 --> 16:58.309
- People call me Slim.
- Ironically, I assume.

16:58.310 --> 16:59.843
Listen, we're looking
for field work,

16:59.844 --> 17:01.645
uh, if you need
any extra hands.

17:01.646 --> 17:03.845
Well, three of our guys
did just get squished,

17:03.846 --> 17:06.062
so we just might.
Come on in.

17:07.230 --> 17:09.447
So, have you done this
kind of work before?

17:09.448 --> 17:11.414
Have we pulled an object
off a plant

17:11.415 --> 17:13.182
and placed it
in a burlap bag?

17:13.183 --> 17:16.183
Yes, I think we understand
the nuances of this profession.

17:16.184 --> 17:18.583
Good, good. And how about you?
Tell me about yourself.

17:18.584 --> 17:21.884
I like to kill animals
and then a lady.

17:21.885 --> 17:25.002
I got a good feeling
about you guys.

17:28.305 --> 17:30.421
All right, you guys
are doing great.

17:30.422 --> 17:32.121
Hey, listen,
my dog just had puppies,

17:32.122 --> 17:35.322
and I thought, since you're covered
with feces and I barely know you,

17:35.323 --> 17:38.357
I'd give you a delicate,
snow-white, newborn puppy.

17:38.358 --> 17:40.291
Okay, just don't give me
to Dead-Eyes over there,

17:40.292 --> 17:41.692
'cause I've already
been killed twice

17:41.693 --> 17:43.226
in the other two stories,
and I don't want...

17:43.227 --> 17:45.059
- Puppy!
- Aw,!

17:47.579 --> 17:49.844
This puppy doesn't work!

17:51.381 --> 17:53.930
Well, well, well...

17:53.931 --> 17:55.797
As you can tell by
the "well, well, well",

17:55.798 --> 17:56.864
he's the bad guy.

17:56.865 --> 17:59.032
Looks like we got us
some new employees.

17:59.033 --> 18:00.865
That's right, Curley,
I hired 'em this morning.

18:00.866 --> 18:02.265
Well, tell 'em to get out.

18:02.266 --> 18:04.966
This is where I practice
my karate, 'cause I'm a dick.

18:04.967 --> 18:07.267
I understand you like
to pick fruit.

18:07.268 --> 18:09.901
You ever pick something
bruised and pear-shaped?

18:09.902 --> 18:12.403
Fruit has seeds you can poo out!

18:12.404 --> 18:14.970
Hey, Hodor, stop coming on
to my slutty wife!

18:14.971 --> 18:17.571
Look, I can tell by the
fact that you wear a single,

18:17.572 --> 18:20.473
Vaseline-filled leather glove
that you're a reasonable man.

18:20.474 --> 18:22.639
So, let's all take a deep
breath and calm down.

18:22.640 --> 18:24.341
No!
Karate chop!

18:28.443 --> 18:29.508
Damn it!

18:29.509 --> 18:31.710
I tuck my jeans into my boots!

18:31.711 --> 18:34.127
I'll get you,
you stupid, giant moron.

18:36.330 --> 18:37.911
Not great timing, I know,

18:37.912 --> 18:40.763
but can I leave early
for a dentist appointment?

18:44.467 --> 18:46.215
So, I should be home by 10:00.

18:46.216 --> 18:48.483
It's just this
piano-bar-slash-cabaret place

18:48.484 --> 18:49.516
called "Tinkles."

18:49.517 --> 18:50.850
Rory told me about it.

18:50.851 --> 18:52.117
Who's Rory?

18:52.118 --> 18:53.318
You remember him.

18:53.319 --> 18:54.917
The field hand who gave me
a shoulder ride

18:54.918 --> 18:55.952
back to the house?

18:55.953 --> 18:57.152
That was Rory.

18:57.153 --> 18:58.986
Anyway, it sounds like
it's just a hoot.

18:58.987 --> 19:03.054
Wow, maybe you'll meet a pretty
lady to get married to there.

19:03.055 --> 19:05.255
Yeah, well, that's the idea.

19:05.256 --> 19:07.789
While you're gone,
can I touch myself?

19:07.790 --> 19:10.290
Uh, again, you don't have
to schedule that with me.

19:10.291 --> 19:11.958
But remember,
if there's any trouble,

19:11.959 --> 19:14.159
we meet by the big tree
on the edge of town.

19:14.160 --> 19:16.559
Everything in my
head is screaming.

19:16.560 --> 19:19.876
All right, then, I am off.

19:23.314 --> 19:24.795
Well, hello there.

19:24.796 --> 19:27.097
If it isn't the sexy imbecile.

19:27.098 --> 19:28.363
Oh, hi.

19:28.364 --> 19:30.931
Sorry about what I did
to your husband earlier.

19:30.932 --> 19:33.766
Yes, that was quite
a hand job you did on him.

19:33.767 --> 19:36.867
You know, I'm not so bad
at those myself.

19:36.868 --> 19:38.134
I'm not gonna lie to you,

19:38.135 --> 19:40.834
you're wasting your
double entendres on me.

19:40.835 --> 19:42.735
I want you to destroy me.

19:42.736 --> 19:43.970
Okay!

19:51.657 --> 19:54.306
♪ Jeepers creepers ♪

19:54.307 --> 19:56.741
♪ Where'd you get
those peepers ♪

19:56.742 --> 19:59.475
♪ Jeepers creepers ♪

19:59.476 --> 20:01.642
♪ Where'd you get those eyes ♪

20:02.977 --> 20:04.377
Thank you, thank you.

20:04.378 --> 20:07.711
Oh, I just love a song that
explains what it just said.

20:10.079 --> 20:12.379
All right, evidently
I have to go to the big tree

20:12.380 --> 20:14.380
on the edge of town
to take care of something.

20:14.381 --> 20:15.380
This shouldn't take too long.

20:15.381 --> 20:18.481
Do not take my songs
off the list.

20:23.201 --> 20:25.885
I'm sorry, George,
I didn't mean to kill the girl,

20:25.886 --> 20:28.585
and now the whole town's
gonna hang me by a rope.

20:28.586 --> 20:30.419
Oh, I would never
let that happen.

20:30.420 --> 20:31.753
Thanks.

20:31.754 --> 20:34.488
- Tell me about the rabbits, George.
- Yeah, sure thing.

20:34.489 --> 20:36.488
But while I do that, why
don't you face away from me

20:36.489 --> 20:37.755
and count the stars.

20:37.756 --> 20:40.256
Okay.

20:40.257 --> 20:43.057
All right, so the B&B will
have a rack of single-gear bikes

20:43.058 --> 20:45.725
for every guest, and yes,
next to that, of course,

20:45.726 --> 20:48.192
is going to be
the big, giant rabbit hutch.

20:48.193 --> 20:49.842
Buh-bye, Lennie.

20:50.879 --> 20:52.027
Goodnight, kids.

20:52.028 --> 20:53.460
Good luck with
those book reports.

20:53.573 --> 20:56.440
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru